  },
  {
   "id": "a02-text-11",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 638,
   "y": 166,
   "width": 958,
   "height": 48,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 87109,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1152019,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "S knows the whole map, so it can check N’s own shortest path to D. All checks use a strict\n\"<\".",
   "originalText": "S knows the whole map, so it can check N’s own shortest path to D. All checks use a strict\n\"<\".",
   "fontSize": 19,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "a02-text-12",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 638,
   "y": 224,
   "width": 788,
   "height": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 95028,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1256748,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "Check                   Inequality                           Example 1, N\n----------------------  -----------------------------------  ---------------------\n1 Loop-free (required)  dist(N,D) < dist(N,S) + dist(S,D)    10 < 15 + 20 = 35  ✓\n2 Downstream            dist(N,D) < dist(S,D)                10 < 20            ✓\n3 Node-protecting       dist(N,D) < dist(N,E) + dist(E,D)    10 < 20 + 10 = 30  ✓",
   "originalText": "Check                   Inequality                           Example 1, N\n----------------------  -----------------------------------  ---------------------\n1 Loop-free (required)  dist(N,D) < dist(N,S) + dist(S,D)    10 < 15 + 20 = 35  ✓\n2 Downstream            dist(N,D) < dist(S,D)                10 < 20            ✓\n3 Node-protecting       dist(N,D) < dist(N,E) + dist(E,D)    10 < 20 + 10 = 30  ✓",
   "fontSize": 16,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "a02-text-13",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 638,
   "y": 334,
   "width": 224,
   "height": 24,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 102947,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1361477,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "What each check means",
   "originalText": "What each check means",
   "fontSize": 19,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "a02-text-14",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 638,
   "y": 368,
   "width": 962,
   "height": 107,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "groupIds": [],
   "frameId": null,
   "roundness": null,
   "seed": 110866,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 1466206,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "boundElements": null,
   "updated": 1,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "1. The right side is N’s cost to D if it went through S. Strictly cheaper ⇒ N doesn’t go back through\n   S, so no loop (B3).\n2. N is closer to D than S. Also stops loops between two routers that both switch to backups at once\n   (B4).\n3. N’s path to D avoids router E, so the backup survives E failing, not only the link (B5).",
   "originalText": "1. The right side is N’s cost to D if it went through S. Strictly cheaper ⇒ N doesn’t go back through\n   S, so no loop (B3).\n2. N is closer to D than S. Also stops loops between two routers that both switch to backups at once\n   (B4).\n3. N’s path to D avoids router E, so the backup survives E failing, not only the link (B5).",
   "fontSize": 17,
   "fontFamily": 2,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "a02-text-15",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 638,
   "y": 485,
   "width": 394,
   "height": 24,
   "angle": 0,
   "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
